      "worked_solution": "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227715/assets/4d340b37161cb3f970ba588fa15a21b3a35ee376c5766e92d6c48358d4ed003e.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {5}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 25 \\\\  & =12.5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
