      "worked_solution": "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right  triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227715/assets/3f9a52834fe76f1560beec8580dbd91076a9f7c6ef980f410aa5bfe7da162c9c.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {20}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 400 \\\\  & =200.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
